{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep, etc., and you shall do them, that you may prosper in all that you do.</b> Since one commandment draws after it another commandment (Avot 4:2), therefore he says that one commandment causes that 'you may prosper in all that you do' — for each one draws its fellow after it. And this is what they said (ibid. 4:2): that the reward of a commandment is a commandment. And this is what it says: 'And you shall keep and you shall do them' — for the keeping (שְׁמִירָה) draws after it the doing (עֲשִׂיָּה), and the reward of the doing is 'that you may prosper' further, in the future, 'in all that you do.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:14:24.689641339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}